  "query_preview": "..\nThe monsoon pattern has shifted north enough to include Guam within\nthe light to moderate westerly wind flow today. As the monsoonal \nflow continues to buckle against the col to the northwest, showers \nwill start to build for Guam, so high-end (50 percent) scattered \nshowers are in store tonight. As for the CNMI, light and variable \nwinds will become moderate westerlies after midnight, with isolated \nshowers at least until Saturday afternoon. Shortly thereafter, all\nislands can expect increasing winds with scattered showers and\nisolated thunderstorms through next week as the monsoon pattern\nintensifies over the region, eventually lifting to the north in the \nlatter half of the week. Now would be a good time to take down \ncanopies and plan outdoor activities accordingly as conditions \ndeteriorate throughout the weekend.",
